/**

@page libdhcp_cb_cmds Kea Config Backend Commands Hooks Library

Welcome to Kea Config Backend Commands Hooks Library. This documentation is
addressed at developers who are interested in internal operation of the
library. This file provides information needed to understand and perhaps
extend this library.

This documentation is stand-alone: you should have read and
understood <a href="https://reports.kea.isc.org/dev_guide/">Kea
Developer's Guide</a> and in particular its section about hooks: <a
href="https://reports.kea.isc.org/dev_guide/df/d46/hooksdgDevelopersGuide.html">
Hooks Developer's Guide</a>.

@section cbCmdsOverview Overview
The @c cb_cmds hooks library provides support for commands to manipulate
Kea configuration information in the databases via the configuration
backends. The server receiving those commands must be configured to use
the configuration backend(s) connected to the database(s) where the
data is stored. Each command may include a "remote" map which specifies
the database where the data should be stored or from which the
data should be fetched.

@section cbCmdsInternals Library Internals

The structure of the library is very simple. The @c cb_cmds_callouts.cc
file contains the command handlers registered during the library
initialization. Each such handler calls respective methods of the
@c ConfigCmdsDhcp4Impl and @c ConfigCmdsDhcp6Impl classes to process
the commands. The @c ConfigCmdsDhcp4Impl and @c ConfigCmdsDhcp6Impl
methods are responsible for extracting the commands from the
provided @c CalloutHandle objects, validating them, running through
the parsers, processing and returning a response within the
@c CalloutHandle object.

When possible, the cb_cmds hooks library uses Kea configuration
parsers (the same that are used to parse configuration information
from the config file) to parse the data carried in the commands.

@section cbCmdsMTCompatibility Multi-Threading Compatibility

The @c cb_cmds hooks library is compatible with multi-threading.
(it is orthogonal to the DHCP service).

*/
